  "scalar_softfloat_contract": "f32/f64 add/sub/mul/div and sqrt only: Apple ARM64 scalar-struct ABI i32 (i64,i64) / i64 (i64,i64) for binary operations; sqrt is i32 (i64) / i64 (i64), exact nonvariadic C declaration/call. Arguments are values, never addresses. Reviewed dependencies use locals, bounded internal tables and host thread-local rounding/exception state. Exact library identity and header contents checked by sse_inputs.",
  "barrier_asm_sources": [
    "port/llasm-support/tribes_sse.c"
  ],
  "barrier_asm_contract": "Only void zero-operand side-effecting dsb sy and isb with exactly a memory clobber inside the source-pinned tb_sse_fence helper. Other assembly stays blocked.",
  "socket_host_contract": "Fixed Darwin i32-returning nonvariadic signatures checked by ExternalMemoryPass: socket(i32,i32,i32), shutdown(i32,i32), getrlimit(i32,ptr), setsockopt(i32,i32,i32,ptr,i32), bind/connect(i32,ptr,i32), getsockname/getpeername(i32,ptr,ptr), getsockopt(i32,i32,i32,ptr,ptr). All pointer arguments must lie outside guest backing. Native Winsock marshals sockaddr/options/length/resource-limit storage into host-owned objects. No ioctl, recvmsg or nested-buffer exemption. Flat Darwin sendto i64(i32,ptr,i64,i32,ptr,i32) and recvfrom i64(i32,ptr,i64,i32,ptr,ptr) require native-owned payload, sockaddr and length storage. Darwin send/recv use the exact i64(i32,ptr,i64,i32) signature with private payload staging; direct guest payload pointers remain rejected.",
  "curl_host_contract": "Exact signatures and finite constant variadic selectors are checked in ExternalMemoryPass. Native callback targets must be registered checked code; all pointer arguments remain host-only. Runtime registries and staged buffers marshal guest handles, strings and output values. curl_version is the separately reviewed allocator-free, static-buffer path of the pinned curl/LibreSSL/zlib backend; it can run before global initialization. Other allocating/lifecycle APIs require an allocator frame.",
  "processor_snapshot_sources": [
    "port/core/guest_system_query.c"
  ],
  "registry_host_contract": "sysctlbyname uses exact Darwin int(ptr,ptr,ptr,ptr,size_t) ABI with null newp and zero newlen. All name/output/length pointers are host-owned; only fixed CPU metadata names are used in the source-bound service. Missing or zero native frequency uses the source-bound, explicitly declared libuv Apple metadata fallback; other host failures remain errors.",
  "scheduling_sources": [
    "port/core/guest_scheduling.c"
  ],
  "scheduling_contract": "Exact Darwin int setpriority(int,id_t,int), restricted to reviewed scheduling service and constant PRIO_PROCESS=0, who=0. No other process/group/user scheduling mutation.",
  "condition_contract": "Exact nonvariadic Darwin i32 pthread_cond_signal(ptr) and i32 pthread_cond_timedwait_relative_np(ptr,ptr,ptr); all direct arguments host-only. Native condition/mutex/timespec storage only, never guest lock words.",
  "thread_contract": "Exact Darwin pthread attributes and _setjmp/_longjmp ABI, host-owned storage only. pthread_create has four host pointers and requires its entry to be a registered AOT target. Guest entries are finite dispatch tokens, never native callback pointers.",
  "sdl_metadata_contract": "Exact bool(i1) return and three/two host string pointers. Guest UTF-8 inputs are checked and copied before native SDL entry; the existing owner-thread guest allocator frame covers all native allocations. Preserve SDL 3.2.18 behavior, including its aggregate metadata setter return on underlying property allocation failure.",
  "font_sources": [
    "port/apple/font.m"
  ]
}
